#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Panimula"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've seen a few examples of quantum error correcting codes in previous lessons of this course, including the 9-qubit Shor code, the 7-qubit Steane code, and the 5-qubit code.\n"
"These codes are undoubtedly interesting and represent a natural place to begin an exploration of quantum error correction, but a problem with them is that they can only tolerate a very low error rate.\n"
"Correcting an error on one qubit out of five, seven, or nine isn't bad, but in all likelihood we're going to need to be able to tolerate a lot more errors than that to make large-scale quantum computing a reality.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakita na natin ang ilang halimbawa ng quantum error correcting codes sa mga nakaraang aralin ng kursong ito, kabilang ang 9-qubit Shor code, ang 7-qubit Steane code, at ang 5-qubit code.\n"
"Walang alinlangan na kawili-wili ang mga code na ito at natural silang panimulang punto sa pag-explore ng quantum error correction, ngunit ang problema sa kanila ay napakababa lang ng error rate na kaya nilang tiisin.\n"
"Hindi naman masama ang mag-correct ng error sa isang qubit sa lima, pito, o siyam, pero malaki ang posibilidad na kailangan nating kayanin ang mas marami pang error kaysa roon para maging katotohanan ang large-scale quantum computing.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we'll take a first look at some more sophisticated quantum "
"error correcting code constructions, including codes that can tolerate a "
"much higher error rate than the ones we've seen so far, and that are viewed "
"as promising candidates for practical quantum error correction.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa araling ito, unang titingnan natin ang ilang mas sopistikadong "
"konstruksyon ng quantum error correcting code, kabilang ang mga code na kaya"
" nilang tiisin ang mas mataas na error rate kaysa sa mga nakita natin noon, "
"at mga itinuturing na promising na kandidato para sa praktikal na quantum "
"error correction.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin with a class of quantum error correcting codes known as *CSS codes*, named for Robert Calderbank, Peter Shor, and Andrew Steane, who first discovered them.\n"
"The CSS code construction allows one to take certain *pairs* of classical error correcting codes and combine them into a single quantum error correcting code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayo sa isang klase ng quantum error correcting codes na kilala bilang *CSS codes*, na ipinangalan kina Robert Calderbank, Peter Shor, at Andrew Steane, na siyang mga unang nakatuklas nito.\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng CSS code construction, maaaring kumuha ng ilang tiyak na *pares* ng classical error correcting codes at pagsamahin ang mga ito sa iisang quantum error correcting code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second part of the lesson is on a code known as the *toric code*.\n"
"This is a fundamental (and truly beautiful) example of a quantum error correcting code that can tolerate relatively high error rates.\n"
"In fact, the toric code isn't a single example of a quantum error correcting code, but rather it's an infinite family of codes, one for each positive integer greater than one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangalawang bahagi ng aralin ay tungkol sa isang code na kilala bilang *toric code*.\n"
"Ito ay isang pangunahing (at tunay na magandang) halimbawa ng isang quantum error correcting code na kayang tiisin ang medyo mataas na error rate.\n"
"Sa katunayan, ang toric code ay hindi isang solong halimbawa ng quantum error correcting code, kundi isang walang katapusang pamilya ng mga code, isa para sa bawat positibong integer na mas malaki sa isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the last part of the lesson, we'll briefly discuss a couple of "
"other families of quantum codes, including *surface codes* (which are "
"closely connected to the toric code) and *color codes*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa huli, sa huling bahagi ng aralin, maikling tatalakayin natin ang ilang "
"iba pang pamilya ng quantum codes, kabilang ang *surface codes* (na malapit "
"na konektado sa toric code) at *color codes*.\n"

